# Limitations

This is isolated functional evidence, not live CLI/provider or Ara-host
validation. It does not establish a cause for any live Ara behavior. The
acceptance performs synchronous cold transcript scans; this result does not
claim a hard latency deadline.

The separate scanner benchmark recorded in [checkpoint-fix.okf](checkpoint-fix.okf)
used a temporary 230879716-byte transcript: first scan 1.485 seconds, traced
Python peak 2471199 bytes, unchanged cached poll 0.000120 seconds, native input
120. Those values are the other task's recorded scanner benchmark, not a live
Ara observation or a new measurement by this acceptance. Changed file
signatures rescan the full file synchronously; bounded memory is not bounded
latency.

No source policy was changed by this acceptance and no commit was created.
The nonshrinking fixture deliberately uses capacity 2000 and baseline 1200 to
show that capacity alone cannot release a same-size 1200-token request.
The principal fixture is baseline 1200 / capacity 1000 / new native input 120.

